{"title":"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be positive real numbers.  Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b311f5688c5c18e520bfe1a9c56906700c3d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3 + 3b^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{b^3 + 3c^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{c^3 + 3a^3}{5c + a} \\ge \\frac{2}{3} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz</a> inequality,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c853ed04ce97a5d53eb2c179cc962c2d9e0af755.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[a(5a + b) + b(5b + c) + c(5c + a)] \\left( \\frac{a^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{b^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{c^3}{5c + a} \\right) \\ge (a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2,\\]\" width=\"580\" height=\"43\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c70b85f9d08ce18cabc92505778450fa22084b5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{b^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{c^3}{5c + a} \\ge \\frac{(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2}{5a^2 + 5b^2 + 5c^2 + ab + ac + bc}.\\]\" width=\"467\" height=\"40\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db15b2d04ba34c80476cc7ef7e6a4a0886d22e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 \\ge ab + ac + bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67539d05946214142c90df1baebf0bcc6fc3875.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2}{5a^2 + 5b^2 + 5c^2 + ab + ac + bc} \\ge \\frac{(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2}{6a^2 + 6b^2 + 6c^2} = \\frac{1}{6} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\\]\" width=\"517\" height=\"40\" />\nHence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b8b46bbae4a04cad9f782369cbd6b469179254.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{b^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{c^3}{5c + a} \\ge \\frac{1}{6} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Again by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df4ba3115174961740e725bbf3e055ee3c95ca60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[b(5a + b) + c(5b + c) + a(5c + a)] \\left( \\frac{b^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{c^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{a^3}{5c + a} \\right) \\ge (a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2,\\]\" width=\"580\" height=\"43\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a091852266f2a5080dcdc2d9bd4f5aabb253c303.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{b^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{c^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{a^3}{5c + a} \\ge \\frac{(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2}{a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + 5ab + 5ac + 5bc}.\\]\" width=\"467\" height=\"41\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db15b2d04ba34c80476cc7ef7e6a4a0886d22e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 \\ge ab + ac + bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c593c978f6e27800e4421768d0df18ee5d7ee1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2}{a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + 5ab + 5ac + 5bc} \\ge \\frac{(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2}{6a^2 + 6b^2 + 6c^2} = \\frac{1}{6} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\\]\" width=\"517\" height=\"40\" />\nHence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54abb3c7c80aa1733717f8d78fa9680a3cf52dc2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{b^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{c^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{a^3}{5c + a} \\ge \\frac{1}{6} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9736e742df8602ada135197c276e1cdd5c4d108c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3 + 3b^3}{5a + b} + \\frac{b^3 + 3c^3}{5b + c} + \\frac{c^3 + 3a^3}{5c + a} \\ge \\frac{1 + 3}{6} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2) = \\frac{2}{3} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\\]\" width=\"517\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Titu's Lemma: The sum of multiple fractions in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f3572d609c6f93238a4cbae6bccbe04616342d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_n^2}{b_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"21\" height=\"41\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> are sequences of real numbers is greater than of equal to the square of the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> divided by the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />, where i is a whole number less than n+1. Titu's Lemma can be proved using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality after multiplying out the denominator of the RHS.\n</p><p>Consider the LHS of the proposed inequality. Split up the numerators and multiply both sides of the fraction by either a or 3a to make the LHS\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb59c991eeec060f418f26510fdcedc497241af0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} \\frac {a^4} {5a^2+ab}+\\sum_{cyc} \\frac {9a^4} {15ac+3a^2}\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"48\" />\n(Cyclic notation is a special notation in which all permutations of (a,b,c) is the summation command.)\n</p><p>Then use Titu's Lemma on all terms: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e6ffd148cf766ae878225a88cdfbd6a8a32a8ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} \\frac {a^4} {5a^2+ab} +\\sum_{cyc} \\frac {9a^4} {15ac+3a^2} \\ge \\frac {16(a^2+b^2+c^2)^2} {8(a^2+b^2+c^2)+16(ab+bc+ca)} \\ge \\frac {16(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)^2}{24(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)} = \\frac{2}{3} (a^2 + b^2 + c^2)\\]\" width=\"807\" height=\"48\" /> owing to the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785b4231507f4c99c93aa4bf203c784e36ccb8f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2 \\ge ab+bc+ca$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"17\" />, which is actually equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585312fcef71b349b70cf1a047d1830de142630e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2 + (b-c)^2 + (c-a)^2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"19\" />!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We proceed to prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52d3a698663e0f197adc851cb5e2dae41a640ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3 + 3b^3}{5a + b} \\ge -\\frac{1}{36} a^2 + \\frac{25}{36} b^2\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>(then the inequality in question is just the cyclic sum of both sides, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b9c8f86b494c420b447b4ab18833e3c7888935.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} (-\\frac{1}{36} a^2 + \\frac{25}{36} b^2) = \\frac{24}{36}\\sum_{cyc} a^2 = \\frac{2}{3} (a^2+b^2+c^2)\\]\" width=\"389\" height=\"47\" />\n)\n</p><p>Indeed, by AP-GP, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/040230a38420df1ebd9c6f4a3b8ed4864046a31c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[41 (a^3 + b^3+b^3) \\ge 41 \\cdot 3 ab^2\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78cc2657bcc406488570de8825696deaaf82a955.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^3 + a^2b \\ge 2 ab^2\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Summing up, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6c8baaba46e8a756ed5f46223336f7a3205ad8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[41a^3 + 83b^3 + a^2 b \\ge 125 ab^2\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>which is equivalent to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524e82b05d73c8c604d6457527696244b5eda9d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[36(a^3 + 3b^3) \\ge (5a + b)(-a^2 + 25b^2)\\]\" width=\"282\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6d32ef86ddf98713b23490465e9be353dfc1fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36(5a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> from both sides, the desired inequality is proved.\n</p><p>--<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Lightest\" title=\"User:Lightest\">Lightest</a> 15:31, 7 May 2012 (EDT)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Cauchy-Schwarz, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd205430dfa38b6aa7aab8207b972ba9b392cfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{cyc} \\dfrac{a^3}{5a + b} + \\dfrac{b^3}{5a + b} + \\dfrac{b^3}{5a + b} + \\dfrac{b^3}{5a + b} \\right) \\ge \\dfrac{\\left( \\sum_{cyc} a^2 + b^2 + b^2 + b^2 \\right)^2}{ \\left( \\sum_{cyc} a(5a + b) + b(5a + b) + b(5a + b) + b(5a + b) \\right) }\\]\" width=\"771\" height=\"72\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd12be6cc3fab31909d40c6674da42903db894d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\dfrac{\\left(4a^2 + 4b^2 + 4c^2\\right)^2}{\\left(8a^2 + 8b^2 + 8c^2\\right) + \\left(16ab + 16bc + 16ca\\right)}\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1a2614c369fe54215fbcd0bcdce724ff9e12c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\ge \\dfrac{16\\left(a^2 + b^2 + c^2\\right)^2}{\\left(8a^2 + 8b^2 + 8c^2\\right) + \\left(8a^2 + 8b^2\\right) + \\left(8b^2 + 8c^2\\right) + \\left(8c^2 + 8a^2\\right)}\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"46\" /> (by AM-GM) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c7c7316e0057962340f7896f96616b0757235b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\dfrac{2}{3}\\left(a^2 + b^2 + c^2\\right)\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"37\" /> as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We note that if we can prove that there exists a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fc8cc7b68f1a1d227dd9c2f94bcd46b8f28bd24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3+3b^3}{5a+b}\\geq xa^2+(\\frac{2}{3}-x)b^2\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"41\" /> for all positive reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, then we are done since both sides are a cyclic sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Note that if we multiply both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> by a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the left and right sides will both multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> (since the numerator on the left will multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/2471a708cb8167c372f2215758379284f3bf332d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> and the denominator will multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. This means that if the inequality is satisfied for an ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, then it is also satisfied for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6b44c5e8cea6ebcee83b63fd1f7f81cc7a8e4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ar,br)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> for any positive real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, without loss of generality we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf590e9abb33aa9776ddc386b1ba6ee7b43fa413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />,and our inequality becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/e/06e6718a41c304a5f8a7c598007fbd66bf40b5fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a^3+3}{5a+1}\\geq a^2x+\\frac{2}{3}-x.\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"41\" /> Expanding this and rearranging we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b203a4bda873d656c86d2c642177179a04c92840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3(1-5x)+a^2(-x)+a(5x-\\frac{10}{3})+x+\\frac{7}{3}\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"373\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a root of the left side, we can factor this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/520f541c8897c940cba7e9c8c253fc7bda812e79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-1)(a^2(1-5x)+a(1-6x)-x-\\frac{7}{3})\\geq0.\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"38\" /> Note that for this to always be nonnegative, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea9a2974d5614f8770ac8f2449db978dedf4320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2(1-5x)+a(1-6x)-x-\\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"249\" height=\"38\" /> be positive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and negative when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca0e3b3ba285808d0db4e2f698887c144059000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, it must have a root at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, so we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is a root and find that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/720fc70b4a48f960bc40450305d578566bd633e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{1}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/720fc70b4a48f960bc40450305d578566bd633e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{1}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />, the expression factors as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e16e2ab63f64605299c1a2567df0ae1d017aec9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)^2(\\frac{41}{36}a+\\frac{83}{36})\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"188\" height=\"38\" /> which obviously is nonnegative for all positive reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so we are done.\n</p><p>~john0512, bronzetruck2016\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea7850559a04eefb485500c15ccd030e2206953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS=\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a^3+3b^3}{5a+b}=\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a^3}{5a+b}+\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{3b^3}{5a+b}=\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a^4}{5a^2+ab}+\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{9b^4}{15ab+3b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"633\" height=\"53\" /> which tells that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f07ccd3becb1a2e2279756ea9a97d5d0d3d791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS\\geq \\frac{(a^2+b^2+c^2)^2}{5(a^2+b^2+c^2)+ab+bc+ac}+\\frac{3(a^2+b^2+c^2)}{(a^2+b^2+c^2)+5(ab+bc+ac)}\\geq (\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{6})(a^2+b^2+c^2)=RHS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"837\" height=\"45\" />, our proof is done\n</p><p>~bluesoul\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\">USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO\" title=\"2012 USAJMO\">2012 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017013704\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.066 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 390/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13938/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.716      1 -total\n 70.29%   11.749      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 28.46%    4.757      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11053:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017013704 and revision id 175015. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}